---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import GuidePage from '../../components/GuidePage.astro';
import VideoSection from '../../components/VideoSection.astro';
import { t } from '../../i18n/ui';
import type { Lang } from '../../i18n/utils';

const lang: Lang = 'en';
---
<Base lang={lang} path="/events/royal/" title="Royal Castle Scramble &amp; Titles" description="The weekly castle capture race: one march per player, turret and reinforcement rules, Sanctuary 6+ occupation, Royal commendation chests, and the full Royal City title system with queue mechanics.">
  <GuidePage title="Royal Castle Scramble &amp; Titles" description="The weekly castle capture race: one march per player, turret and reinforcement rules, Sanctuary 6+ occupation, Royal commendation chests, and the full Royal City title system with queue mechanics." lang={lang}>
    <p>Royal Castle Scramble is the <strong>weekly castle capture</strong>: alliances race to take and hold the Royal Castle, on the <strong>same weekday and time each week</strong>. The castle fight itself is fast and simple — the preparation (marches, reinforcements, Sanctuary levels) is where matches are decided.</p>
    <p>This guide covers the capture rules, reinforcement mechanics, commendation chests, and the full Royal City title system that the winning kingdom unlocks.</p>

    <h2 id="how-it-works">How It Works</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Weekly</strong>, same weekday and same time every week — set your alarm once and it never changes.</li>
      <li><strong>One march per player.</strong> You get a single march for the whole event.</li>
      <li><strong>It cannot be sped up.</strong> No speedups, no acceleration items — the march speed you march with is the march speed that lands.</li>
      <li><strong>Rallies are recommended.</strong> One march per player makes every march count; rallies pool the alliance&apos;s marches into a single credible attack instead of a stream of solo casualties.</li>
      <li><strong>The initial march is a race.</strong> First marches decide who is sieging and who is scrambling — march timing at the opening whistle matters more than raw power.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="turrets-and-positioning">Turrets and Positioning</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Turrets do NOT activate</strong> in the Scramble — those are <a href="/events/kvk/">KvK</a> mechanics only. There is no turret screen to fight through here.</li>
      <li><strong>Port to the mud</strong> if you are not worried about attacks — <strong>no shield is needed</strong> there. The mud area is the safe staging ground; use it.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="capture-and-reinforcement">Capture and Reinforcement</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>4 hours to take the castle.</strong> Occupation ticks up over the window — it fills <strong>faster with a high occupation percentage</strong> and <strong>slower when contested</strong> by defenders fighting back.</li>
      <li><strong>Reinforcement limit: 30 people</strong> on the castle. That is the hard cap — plan the reinforcement list before the fight, not during it.</li>
      <li><strong>Reinforcements get chipped.</strong> Defenders bleed your garrison down — <strong>pull out and re-reinforce</strong> to reset the chip. A reinforcement at 20% HP is worth less than a fresh body in that slot.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="who-takes-vs-farms">Who Takes, Who Farms</h2>
    <blockquote>Castle takers must be Sanctuary 6+ — everyone else farms resource tiles for points.</blockquote>
    <p>Only <strong>Sanctuary 6+</strong> players can occupy the castle. The split defines your role:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Sanctuary 6+</strong>: march for the castle, rally, reinforce the 30 slots.</li>
      <li><strong>Everyone else</strong>: farm resource tiles around the castle for event points — your march still earns, just not on the walls.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Check your Sanctuary level <strong>before</strong> the event starts; a Sanctuary 5 player marching on the castle wastes the one march they get.</p>

    <h2 id="commendation-chests">Royal Commendation Chests</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>R5 only</strong> — the alliance leader claims by <strong>clicking the castle after the battle</strong>.</li>
      <li><strong>Eligibility: in the kingdom for more than 24 hours.</strong> Players who crossed into the kingdom less than a day before the fight do not count for the chest.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="royal-titles">Royal City Titles</h2>
    <p>Winning the castle unlocks the kingdom&apos;s title system — timed percentage buffs applied by the title holders:</p>
    <table class="w-full mb-6 text-sm">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Title</th><th>Buff type</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Research speed</td><td>Timed % buff to research</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Territory development</td><td>Timed % buff to territory</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Training</td><td>Timed % buff to troop training</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Healing</td><td>Timed % buff to healing</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Minister of the Inner Court</td><td>Farm production buff</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>The queue mechanics:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Queue system</strong> — players line up per title slot, first come first served.</li>
      <li><strong>Each slot runs 5 minutes.</strong></li>
      <li><strong>Mail arrives at the start and end</strong> of your slot, so you know exactly when your buff began and ended.</li>
      <li><strong>Reapply immediately when your slot ends</strong> — the same title can be re-queued, with <strong>no limit on reapplications</strong>. Back-to-back slots are the intended pattern.</li>
      <li><strong>20-minute cooldown after applying</strong> — the one brake on the queue. Time your reapply around it.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Title buffs compound with everything else in the weekly calendar — a research title slot during <a href="/events/alliance-duel/">Alliance Duel Phase 3</a> or a training slot during <a href="/events/alliance-duel/">Phase 5</a> is the calendar double-dip the whole week is built around.</p>

    <VideoSection topic="royal" lang={lang} />
  </GuidePage>
</Base>
